The legal text is the Constitution of Saint Lucia as published in the Revised Laws of Saint Lucia (2023) by the
Attorney General's Chambers of Saint Lucia (https://www.attorneygeneralchambers.com). The site states no licence.
Under the Copyright Act of Saint Lucia (Cap. 13.07), section 24(4) and (5), copyright in works made or first
published by or under the direction of the Government belongs initially to the Crown. The text is reproduced
without change to its wording, as a public record of the law, with attribution to its publisher.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
the amendment notes printed under each provision were left out. The text was arranged as a git commit.
Lexifina does not claim the Attorney General's Chambers endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
